opment. It is essential to point out that the pronounced XRD peak observed in co-doped nanoparticles signifies a diminutive crystallite size and, consequently, an extensive extent of surface. The X3 nanoparticle sizes are greater than that of P, as seen in Fig.  3 a,b, suggesting that its surface morphology is of greater significance. Further, better photodegradation efficiency requires a greater surface area on the sample 63 , 64 . Fig. 4 ( a  &  b ) The TEM images and their corresponding SAED patterns for P and X3 (Inset of Figure ( a  &  b )).

